<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "borg-backup-ui">
<!ENTITY author    "Thorsten Steinberg">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.08.02.1320">
<!ENTITY github    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/borgforge/borg-backup-ui">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&github;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY bootdir   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pkgurl    "&github;/main/releases/&name;-&version;.txz">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        launch="Settings/borg-backup-ui"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        description="Web UI for Borg Backup – Dashboard, Jobs, Storage, History, Restore Tests and Settings. No pip required, pure Python 3."
        icon="plugin-icon.png">

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[
###2026.08.02.1320###
- Fixed the Unraid control page so applying a changed port or bind address restarts Borg Backup UI and redirects to the correct UI URL with the configured port instead of leaving the browser on a blank Settings page.

###2026.08.01.2317###
- The Job Wizard now removes deleted Docker containers from saved runtime selections when the current Docker inventory is available, so stale names no longer stay invisibly selected.

###2026.08.01.1908###
- Issue #322: Allow libvirt VM source paths
- The Job Wizard now accepts `/etc/libvirt` as an explicit source path for Unraid VM backup jobs.
- `/mnt/user/system/libvirt` remains supported through the existing `/mnt` source path handling.
- Fixes duplicate Storagebox repository status text in the Job Wizard preview.
- Uses a cleaner minimal status icon set for repository maintenance cards.
- Aligns System Health & Migration status icons with the minimal status icon set.
- Aligns setup wizard checklist status icons with the minimal status icon set.
- Aligns remaining restore and startup maintenance status markers with the minimal status icon set.
- Issue #329: Fixed the Apprise reminder diagnostics table hover background for taller overdue backup rows.
- Issue #331: Added subtle colored dashboard summary surfaces for faster status scanning.
- Issue #332: Cleaned up the sidebar footer and added a direct light/dark theme toggle without saving backup.conf.
- Issue #333: Replaced the browser restore history delete prompt with an application modal.
- Issue #334: Reorganized the About page around project information and grouped maintainer contact details separately.
- Browse & Restore now respects repository resource locks: browse, download checks, and prechecks report a busy repository clearly, while restore extraction and direct downloads hold the repository lock so matching backup jobs do not start concurrently.
- Restore-held repository locks no longer make the related backup job appear as if a backup run itself was active on the Jobs page.
- Backup starts that are skipped because a restore holds the repository lock are shown as skipped in the live log instead of as failed jobs.
- The Job Wizard now supports a Docker exclusion mode that stops all running containers except the selected containers, making large Appdata backup setups easier to configure.
- Fixed the backup runner so the Docker exclusion mode is preserved at execution time instead of falling back to stopping all containers.

###2026.07.28.0850###
- Added a safe migration-backup cleanup under System Health & Migration: inactive pre-beta migration snapshots can be removed completely, active migrations keep the latest five snapshots, and unknown or protected snapshots are skipped.
- Prevented the canonical backup.conf migration from creating a new migration snapshot just because an installer-created legacy backup.conf.example copy exists while backup.conf already matches the current schema.
- Fixed System Health & Migration so cleanup audit entries are not mistaken for failed migration runs after old migration backups are deleted.
- Fresh installations now require the main data directory to be confirmed in Settings before operational actions are unlocked, instead of silently creating the suggested `/mnt/user/borg-backup-ui` path.
- Config Backups & Rollback now shows diff colors from backup to active configuration, so new active lines are green and removed backup-only lines are red.
- Added third-party license notices for the bundled Apprise notification runtime and its pinned Python dependencies.
- Added the full MIT project license to the repository and packaged plugin payload.
- Added a dedicated Settings > About license page with project and third-party license viewers.
- Improved the repository import browser so existing Borg repositories are detected as selectable endpoints and their internal folders are no longer offered for navigation.
- Issue #310: Added a first-run setup wizard for the required main data directory and the first backup path.
- Fresh installations now clearly guide users through storage target, repository, backup job, and optional restore/notification setup without silently creating objects.
- When storage targets, repositories, or jobs are opened from the setup wizard, successful saves now return to the wizard with refreshed progress.
- Skipped optional setup steps remain visible as dashboard action items so users can continue later.
- Issue #313: Dashboard backup status now marks missed scheduled backup runs as overdue instead of leaving the last successful run displayed as OK.
- Overdue detection uses the configured backup tolerance window and the latest backup status data, so normal runtime delays do not immediately trigger a warning.
- Issue #315: Clarified the About page so BorgBackup version and license information are shown under third-party components instead of Borg Backup UI project metadata.
- Issue #317: Improved About license layout
- The third-party license entries on the About page now use compact cards instead of stretched table-like rows.
- BorgBackup compatibility information is shown as a secondary note in the BorgBackup third-party entry.
- Issue #319: Clearer restore start confirmation
- The final restore wizard step now highlights the explicit confirmation checkbox before starting a restore.
- The confirmation text now explains that checking the box enables the restore start button.

###2026.07.24.1513###
- The startup script now defers Borg Backup UI startup to a background wait when the Unraid Python 3 plugin is not available yet, avoiding false missing-python errors without blocking the remaining boot sequence.
- The weekly HTML report now includes a seven-day activity view. Scheduled jobs show a compact status matrix against their cron plan, while manual jobs are listed separately without being marked as missed.
- The Job Wizard no longer offers direct SMB mount actions. SMB targets must be prepared through SMB profiles and Repository Manager before a job selects an existing repository.
- Repository imports now show a Borg compatibility note because the original Borg version of an existing repository cannot be detected reliably.
- Required fields in the Job, Restore and Repository wizards and key settings forms are now marked consistently so users can see mandatory input before submitting.
- Issue #287: Repository import compatibility notice
- The repository import dialog now explains that Borg Backup UI uses the active Borg 1.4.x runtime and cannot reliably detect the original Borg version of an imported repository.
- The notice asks users to verify older repositories with `borg info` and preferably `borg check` before importing them.
- Issue #289: Repository info refresh controls
- Added a Settings > Repository area for controlling automatic repository information refreshes.
- Automatic repository info refresh can now be disabled to avoid waking spun-down Unraid array disks only for cached repository statistics.
- The refresh worker now schedules the next global run instead of waking every hour to check whether repository statistics are due.
- Settings show the worker state, plugin PID, last run, next run, latest result counts and optional per-repository details without running Borg commands.
- Repository refresh settings are shown under Operations > Repositories with grouped repository details by location.
- USB and SMB repositories whose storage is currently not mounted are treated as warnings and keep the normal refresh interval instead of triggering short error retries.
- Repository details now use consistent grouped table widths, clearer worker status labels and a single Operations menu group.
- The repository refresh enablement control is now a switch and saves immediately when toggled.
- Issue #291: Reliable backup.conf rollback timestamps
- Config backup history now shows the snapshot creation time instead of the copied source file modification time.
- Existing backup.conf rollback snapshots without readable metadata fall back to the timestamp embedded in the backup filename.
- The rollback table labels the timestamp column as Created and clarifies the German reason column as the snapshot trigger instead of the currently displayed diff reason.
- Canonical backup.conf migrations now also create a visible Config Backups & Rollback entry with the `canonical_backup_conf_v1 applied` trigger.
- Restore settings now use the same card surface as the other settings areas instead of falling back to the older darker panel background.
- Fixed a Settings frontend error that could appear when the repository import compatibility notice was refreshed before the Repository Manager DOM element was available.
- Scheduled restore tests with a latest failed, unavailable or unreadable result now remain due immediately, so "Run due tests now" no longer skips them just because the failed manual test was recent.

###2026.07.22.1637###
- Support logs are quieter by default: routine successful polling requests are suppressed, slow or write requests stay visible, and transient Python startup delays during Unraid boot no longer leave false missing-Python errors.
- Support logs now include richer sanitized context for important actions, including job runs, restore tests, storage and repository operations, Apprise profile actions and migration maintenance blockers.
- Backup and restore-test runs now write compact lifecycle summaries to the support log, covering request, process start, final status and notification delivery without duplicating detailed Borg output.
- SMB profiles now get a managed mount path under `/mnt/borg-backup-ui/smb/`, can be mounted or unmounted manually from settings, and can be mounted directly in the job wizard so existing repositories are selectable before saving the job.

###2026.07.21.1712###
- Finalizes canonical configuration ownership for global settings, storage targets and repositories, including an audited startup migration for existing installations.
- Restores archive browsing, information refreshes, tests and maintenance for repositories explicitly configured without encryption while retaining Borg's safety check for unknown repositories.
- Separates the immutable migration execution time from later startup checks and presents recorded migration actions in a readable audit view.
- Apprise event delivery now uses a durable background queue so slow or unavailable providers do not block backup, restore-test or reminder processing.
- Queued Apprise notifications keep per-profile retry and backoff settings, survive application restarts and record sanitized delivery status for troubleshooting and support bundles.
- Added a dedicated Notifications settings area with Apprise profile management, compact saved-profile summaries, searchable provider selection, dynamic provider URL templates from Apprise metadata, URL validation and test delivery.
- Apprise profile editing now generates provider-specific URL fields from the selected URL format, saves non-secret fields for later edits and keeps password/token values write-only so they can be replaced without being rendered back into the browser.
- Provider URL format selection now exposes all Apprise templates so later ntfy formats with password or token fields can be selected during profile creation.
- Saved Apprise profiles now use a quieter compact summary and avoid duplicate provider labels such as `ntfy (ntfy)`.
- Apprise profiles now receive their selected backup, restore-test and overdue reminder events, using the profile display name as the notification title prefix.
- Existing native ntfy settings are migrated into an Apprise profile during startup, and the separate native ntfy settings UI has been removed.
- Migrated Apprise ntfy profiles now reopen the matching URL-format editor correctly, including token-based templates.
- The Notifications settings area no longer shows the one-time ntfy migration note after the cutover.
- Backup and reminder logs now report delivered Apprise profile names instead of showing the inactive native ntfy channel in the standard event summary.
- The canonical `backup.conf` migration now rechecks completed installations after schema updates, so obsolete native ntfy keys and new Apprise keys are cleaned up automatically on startup.
- Validating an existing Apprise profile now uses the stored write-only URL when no replacement URL was entered, matching the test-notification behavior.
- Improved plugin upgrades so an unchanged package is reused or skipped after version and checksum checks, with clearer install output before downloads and long package operations.
- Apprise is now shipped as a verified vendor bundle and only extracted again when the bundled Apprise version or SHA256 changes.
- Fixed the canonical storage migration so legacy SMB profiles with invalid old mount paths are normalized to the managed `/mnt/borg-backup-ui/smb/<profile-key>` mount path instead of blocking startup migration.

###2026.07.18.0057###
- Restore tests now support unencrypted Borg repositories without requiring a passphrase file.

###2026.07.16.1604###
- Rebuilt the bilingual in-app help and complete German and English user manuals with searchable chapter navigation and offline access inside the application.
- Running backup jobs can now be cancelled cooperatively from the Jobs page while Docker and VM recovery remains protected and visible.
- Running restore tests now reopen their live log automatically after the page is loaded or refreshed.
- Updated the German and English user-manual screenshots to the current light-theme interface, restored numbered guide callouts and removed environment-specific SSH profile values.

###2026.07.15.1415###
- Added a read-only Homepage dashboard widget for backup, restore-test, overdue and active-run status with a dedicated restricted token.
- Homepage widget settings can create, rotate or revoke the token and provide a ready-to-copy Custom API configuration.
- Backup cleanup now attempts Docker and VM recovery, status persistence and lock release independently, even if an earlier cleanup step fails.
- Jobs, repository passphrases and profile-secret exports now use a versioned authenticated format with manipulation detection.
- Wrong passwords, modified, damaged and unsupported export files now produce actionable errors before import data is written.
- Failed preview attempts clear previously loaded preview data before another import can be applied.
- Existing encrypted exports remain importable as an explicitly marked legacy format; all new exports use the authenticated format.

###2026.07.14.1342###
- Security and access control:
  - Static UI paths, log streams, restore downloads and repository streams now enforce path containment, authentication and role checks.
  - Corrupt user data fails closed instead of reopening administrator setup.
- Backup and recovery safety:
  - Jobs stop before Docker, VM or Borg operations when a required source path is missing and report every affected path.
  - VM recovery verifies that the VMs stopped by the job were restarted and keeps failures visible.
  - Repository maintenance waits up to 30 seconds for transient Borg locks and provides privacy-safe troubleshooting guidance.
- User interface:
  - New users follow the browser or operating-system theme by default, and dark-theme secondary text has improved contrast.
- Issue #223:
  - SMB profiles now negotiate modern SMB 2/3 automatically by default.
  - SMB profile checks provide actionable diagnostics for protocol, authentication, permissions, share and network failures.

###2026.07.13.2248###
- Issue #205:
  - Repository creation and import now validate targets before writing and report actionable conflicts.
  - Editing a job preserves its schedule and reports persistence errors without closing the wizard.
- Issue #208:
  - SSH keepalives are applied consistently to backups, repository maintenance, restores and restore tests.
  - Interrupted SSH connections now report a clear network error without implying repository corruption.
- Issue #186:
  - Existing repositories can be selected through a storage-scoped directory browser for Local, USB, SMB and SSH targets.
- Issue #206:
  - Backup source paths now preserve spaces through structured JSON arrays.
  - Existing jobs are migrated once with audit, rollback backup and clear diagnostics for ambiguous legacy values.

###2026.07.13.1144###
- Upgrade notice:
  - Back up /boot/config/borg-backup before installing this release.
  - Existing storage targets, repositories and jobs are migrated once to the canonical data model. Review the migration result under Settings > System Health & Migration after restart.
- Repository and storage management:
  - Jobs now select centrally managed repositories on storage targets configured under Settings.
  - Repositories can be created, imported, inspected, maintained, removed from the inventory or permanently deleted through guarded workflows.
  - Persistent Borg keyfiles, repository passphrases and lifecycle audit records are handled centrally.
- Backup workflow:
  - The Job Wizard supports source exclusions, improved path selection and clearer storage/repository assignment.
  - Dashboard rows are grouped by storage location and long Docker/VM selections remain contained inside the Wizard.
- Safety and maintenance:
  - Canonical migrations are audited, idempotent and protected by rollback backups and consistency checks.
  - A guarded factory reset, improved runtime recovery diagnostics and localized blocker messages were added.
  - The Unraid plugin icon opens the Borg Backup UI control panel under Settings.

###2026.07.05.1531###
